[Music]  welcome back to CBS morning's when  Senator Rafael Warnock won his runoff  election earlier this month his victory  cemented Democrats control of the U.S  Senate the Baptist pastor won his first  full six-year term after previously  winning a special election for the seat  back in 2021. now he is the first black  American to represent Georgia in the  Senate and the first black Democrat  elected to the Chamber from a Southern  state senator Warnock joins us now for  an exclusive interview on CBS morning's  Senator welcome and congratulations to  you good morning great to be here with  you so was Herschel Walker the first  call you received on Election night well  I I didn't hear from from him but listen  I'm still I'm proud of what the people  of Georgia have done yeah they certainly  came through for you they look my name  has been on the ballot five times in  less than three years  for the same doggone job clearly I  wanted this job because it allows me to  continue what's been my lifelong project  but this race seems to be we'll talk  about your your goals in a second but  the races seem to be closer than people  expected considering your opponent  considering the times what do you say  about that and Stacy Abrams did not win  the the gubernatorial seat well these  races are hard fought and it wasn't long  ago you know that we were looking at a  different situation in Georgia I'm the  first uh Democrat uh elected alongside  John ossoff in about 20 years to the  Senate and so this race is a hard fought  but we continue to build on the progress  that we've been able to make over the  years and I'm honored that I get to use  that influence that the people of  Georgia have placed in my hands you know  I think about this all the time it's  really it's an amazing thing for the  people of your state to say when we  think about our families yeah when we  look into the eyes of our children as we  try to take care of our parents as they  deal with both the blessings and the  burdens of Aging we'd like for you to  represent us uh in the senate for me  that's a sacred trust it's something I  take seriously and I'm honored to do  that clearly you keep coming back to the  job as voter suppression's still an  issue though in Georgia oh absolutely we  we should some people could say look he  won that's no longer an argument we  should not assume that because I won  that voter suppression is not an issue  in Georgia in fact I had to sue  the state of Georgia so that we could  get Saturday voting they they shortened  the runoff uh and then they said the  Saturday after a holiday which was  Thanksgiving and another Holiday by the  way that uh honored confederal  confederate general uh lee they said we  couldn't have we couldn't have Saturday  voting so I had to sue them they  appealed it took two additional appeals  to secure Saturday voting and then the  people of Georgia showed up they built a  senator a multi-racial coalition of  Consciousness  but Senator I mean it's not just some  people who could say you won so voter  suppression is not the problem it was  it's Brad rafsenberger who's the  Secretary of State of Georgia he's got  an op-ed in the Wall Street Journal out  today uh he's famed for many of our  viewers for standing up to Donald  Trump's claims of denying the election  or that the election was was stolen he's  now calling you an election denier  saying you can't say it's not a free and  fair election if you've got record  turnout what do you say to that the fact  that people have had to overcome  barriers doesn't mean those barriers  don't exist we literally saw college  students and seniors and lines that were  hours and hours and hours long  maybe he's happy with that I'm not I  think we can do better than that your  vote is your voice your voice is your  human dignity there's nothing more  sacred  than the right to vote you can have the  right to vote and still not have access  and so that's the work that I've been  doing for a long time long before I ran  for office yeah because the vote for me  as I often say is a kind of prayer for  the world we desire for ourselves and  for our children which is why I'm  focused now as a legislator on passing  voting rights in our Congress  speaking of Elections um you mentioned  during the commercial break there is a  fascination with the next election sure  do you believe that President Biden  should run for reelection in 2024. oh I  think if if he chooses to run I will  support him but I I do think we spend so  much time in our country focused on the  next election and we're not thinking  often enough about the Next Generation  yeah I was doing this work long before I  ran for office and I think that the  people are well served by politicians  are not well served by politicians who  make the politics about them of course  it ought to be about the hard-working  people of Georgia who are trying to keep  the promises that all of us make to our  children are you going to be the  president of the United States listen my  name's been on the ballot five times  in three years and so uh after that uh  I'm finally focused on being able to do  the work the people of Georgia have  elected me to do in addition to that  I've got two children at home yeah a  little little guys let's talk about a  trip to Disney World well I think you  can deliver on that let's talk about the  January 6 committee is ready it seems to  recommend that Donald Trump be  prosecuted to be held accountable what  do you think should happen there I know  it's it's a recommendation and it's  their decision but what do you think  should happen I think we are a nation of  laws and not of men  and so uh it's important that we protect  our election system again the people of  Georgia sent me to the Senate alongside  John also the first African-American and  first Jew on January 5th on January 6 we  saw the most violent assault that we've  seen since the War of 1812 on our  Capital driven by the big lie we all saw  it so you think he should be prosecuted  I think that this committee has done  excellent work and I've been that's a  yes or no question Senator yes sir I'm  saying that we as they refer to the  Department of Justice we want to allow  the Department of Justice to do its work  all right and and no one should be above  the law nobody  uh on the border right now uh the  administration is warning of a potential  increase in the already increased  numbers of people showing up because of  a title 42 expiring title 42 is allows  the government to expel migrants for um  for public health reasons uh do you  think it's a mistake given the lack of  resources on the border given the crush  of people coming to let it expire do you  think we need title 42 to control the  Border I think it's important to secure  the border which I've always said  and I think it's important that people  have a dignified orderly path to  citizenship which I've always said we  are a nation of immigrants  and I think it's only politics  that creates this false choice between  securing the Border yeah and giving  people a dignified path to citizenship  and by the way doing something about the  dreamers  uh for whom this is the only country  they've ever known and those who are  dealing with temporary protective status  right now I think we can do both of  those things at the same time we need  comprehensive immigration reform in this  country I know we've been saying that  we've been saying that for years and  years and years and that never changes  can you imagine well so far it hasn't  changed can you imagine a scenario where  we say look I'm so sorry we just can't  help you we don't have the resources we  don't have the spaces we don't have the  manpower to help can you can you  envision that I think we are a nation of  immigrants and we always will be we are  great not in spite of our diversity but  because of it and again we can secure  the Border we have to make sure that we  don't make a humanitarian crisis at the  board a worse  while at the same time we can forge a  path I believe a bipartisan path you do  to getting immigration reform done in  our country and  um people who are in business farmers  and folks in the agriculture sector and  other sectors know that that we've got  to do these things yeah and I remain  focused on it Senator Warnock you don't  have to run for anything now for six  years  otherwise I'm running to Disney World  with my two little children here it is  but before that I'm going to take a nap  all right we got a comfortable couch  tonight  thank you very much appreciate it

